# UNSURE -- an OPEN QUESTION, recorded rather than guessed. trap-codes.md says
# T_DivByZero is "a / or % with a zero divisor" WITHOUT qualifying the operand
# type, so this expectation follows the registry: a loud failure. IEEE-754 would
# instead say +inf, and `float` is documented as IEEE 64-bit. Whichever way the
# owner ratifies it, one of the two documents must change.
# Expected: the program must not print "after"; it should fail loudly.
float zero():
    return 0.0

void main():
    print("before")
    float q = 1.0 / zero()
    print(f"{q}")
    print("after")
